#   question: is the DPU's run-6 map of REG_0 byte 0x7B (shift_bias << 2 | 1) a property of the AIE2 bias upshift itself?
#   static trace (PDI 2 = graph_used_pdi_list [2], scratch pm/pm_0002_c0r3.s, a READING AID with no pipeline-timing model):
#     0x2274 lda.s8 r5, [p3, 0x20]: a SIGNED byte load from offset 0x20 of a param struct whose offset 0x21 feeds the conv's
#     output vsrs (0x228a lda.s8 r22, [p3, 0x21] -> s0 -> vsrs.d8.s32 next to vmac). 0x22e0 mov s3, r5; 0x24d4
#     vlda.2d.ups.s32.s8 cm4, s3, [p6] (int8 vector upshifted into acc32 by s3). So the bias upshift's scalar is plausibly
