# POST-HOC (scratch ups_model.py, sha256 4e725d8db29b0ed35d7e02d76cdf9ce34ea9f64614311ce768e2c33a8671f8e9), fitted on this same data:
    points 384, model k = s & 63 (saturating) misses 0, points read as all-zero 0
#   Native vups reads k = s & 63 as an unsigned LEFT shift, saturating to 32 bits, at all 384 scalars. Unlike vsrs,
#   codes 60..63 do not shift the other way. k >= 31 saturates every nonzero lane, so those codes are not
#   separated from each other. No scalar zeroed the lanes, and none shifts right. So the DPU's bit-7 outcome
#   (no bias, or a bias right-shifted by 8 or more) cannot come from vups with any scalar: for those bytes the
#   overlay skips or reroutes the bias. Why 0x81 is the exception stays UNEXPLAINED, now pinned to the overlay's
#   decode code.
